WEBVTT

00:35:26.406 --> 00:35:31.449
Free-market economics doesn't give you
a way to moralize the market.

00:35:31.473 --> 00:35:35.670
We're moral creatures. And if you put us
in an amoral system, we will rebel.

00:35:35.694 --> 00:35:37.605
That's sort of what's happening now.

00:35:37.629 --> 00:35:41.230
And I think what young conservatives
are doing is trying to find that thing,

00:35:41.254 --> 00:35:42.937
that moral market, that sense that,

00:35:42.961 --> 00:35:46.405
"Capitalism is great, but we've got to
put it within social constraints."

00:35:46.429 --> 00:35:49.008
CA: But when you think
about community, is it --

00:35:49.032 --> 00:35:51.396
what would you say to someone who said,

00:35:51.420 --> 00:35:54.207
"I believe in community,
but I also believe this,

00:35:54.231 --> 00:36:00.531
that community depends on,
to some extent, deep roots of tradition.